#maps
stack_master/maps/*
!stack_master/maps/GLC_smile_small
stack_master/maps/GLC_smile_small/speed_scaling.yaml
stack_master/maps/GLC_smile_small/ot_sectors.yaml
!stack_master/maps/hangar_1905_v0
# speed_scaling.yaml / ot_sectors.yaml are tracked for this map: they are drawn by
# hand in the sector_slicer GUI and the map is unusable without them
# (ot_interpolator dies on a missing n_sectors, state_machine then waits forever
# for scaled global waypoints). The same two files are already tracked for
# GLC_smile_small and glc_ot_ez.

# The skku_track_22x8 family is synthetic -- scripts/sketch_to_map.py draws it
# from a committed sketch, so unlike the recorded maps above there is no machine
# it lives on. Tracked so it survives a fresh clone. The three suffixed maps are
# the same centre line at different per-sector widths; see
# skku_track_22x8/width_variants.png.
!stack_master/maps/skku_track_22x8
!stack_master/maps/skku_track_22x8_wide
!stack_master/maps/skku_track_22x8_mid
!stack_master/maps/skku_track_22x8_narrow
# Screenshots and previews are working files, not part of any map.
stack_master/maps/*/rviz_timetrials.png
stack_master/maps/*/preview_*.png

